---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/content/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const path = '/cookies/';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Notice"
  description="How DocuForge Tools uses cookies for optional analytics with Consent Mode v2. Generators work without cookies."
  path={path}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Cookies', path }]} />
  <h1>Cookie notice</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Our document generators do not require cookies to fill forms, preview documents, or export PDF/DOCX.
    Everything in the editor runs in your browser.
  </p>
  <h2>Analytics and Consent Mode</h2>
  <p>
    If Google Analytics (GA4) is configured, we load it only after you accept the cookie bar (or if you
    previously accepted). Until then, Google Consent Mode v2 defaults keep <code>analytics_storage</code>
    denied. The GA script is deferred until after page load / idle so it is not render-blocking.
  </p>
  <p>
    Accepting stores <code>docuforge:cookie-ok</code> in localStorage on this device. Clearing site data
    will show the bar again.
  </p>
  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Google AdSense is off unless explicitly enabled in site configuration. When enabled for EEA/UK
    traffic, a certified CMP should be added per Google’s requirements. See the
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Use browser settings to block or delete cookies. For personalized ads from Google, visit
    <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ad Settings</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
